== 4. Proposition 6.1 arithmetic ==
   odd n in [1025, 3*10^6]: failures 0; n - 3h takes the values [0, 2, 4]; least h = 341 (at n = 1025: h = 341)
   base range: largest odd n below 1025 is 1023 = 3 * 341, so the base 'all odd numbers below 1024' is exactly what the step needs
== 5. Proposition 5.1 ==
   mu_1..mu_6 = ['1', '1', '3/2', '3', '15/2', '45/2'] ; nondecreasing from n=1: True ; strictly increasing from n=2: True ; mu_1 = mu_2: True
   for n = 3..12 and every odd h in (mu_(n-1), mu_n]: mu_(n-1) < h <= E_(1/2)[H_n], so by strict monotonicity the tilt lies in [1/2, p_n): True
   note: p_n is undefined at n = 2 (E_p[H_2] = 1 for all p) and p_3 = 1 (mu_2 = 1); the hypothesis needs n_0 >= 3
